  "title": "Erdős Problem #653",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\in \\mathbb{R}^2$ and let $R(x_i)=\\#\\{ \\lvert x_j-x_i\\rvert : j\neq i\\}$, where the points are ordered such that $ R(x_1)\\leq \\cdots \\leq R(x_n). $ Let $g(n)$ be the maximum number of distinct values the $R(x_i)$ can take. Is it true that $g(n) \\geq (1-o(1))n$?",
